  "Number": 16,
  "Question": "What is the value of the following expression?\n\n\\[\\cfrac{1}{1 + \\cfrac{1}{2 + \\cfrac{1}{3}}}\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac16\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{3}{10}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{7}{10}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac56\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{10}{3}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Start with the innermost denominator, since its value determines the fraction above it:\n\\[\n2+\\frac13=\\frac73.\n\\]\nDividing \\(1\\) by a nonzero fraction gives its reciprocal, with numerator and denominator interchanged. Thus the middle fraction is \\(\\frac37\\). The outer denominator becomes\n\\[\n1+\\frac37=\\frac{10}{7}.\n\\]\nTaking its reciprocal gives\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{10/7}=\\frac7{10}.\n\\]\nAll the denominators used are positive. The value is \\(\\frac7{10}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
